WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:03.490
Where do Jeff Bezos and Richard Branson

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:06.370
get off spending their
own money to go into space

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.320
when we already have a scandal-ridden,

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.780
and incompetent public
agency for that very purpose?

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.080
All Richard Branson ever did
was give away half his fortune

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.880
after foisting Tubular Bells

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.770
and the Sex Pistols on the world.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.610
All Jeff Bezos ever did was make

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.700
a year-long pandemic bearable

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.930
by creating the company
that delivered everything

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.270
we wanted to our doors within hours.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:29.730
Maybe Elon Musk is a welfare queen,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.010
but as long as he's
spending his own Doge Coin

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:36.560
and living in a $50,000 prefab
house, who are we to judge?

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.160
If AOC's former policy guy is right

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.950
that every billionaire
is a policy failure,

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.600
then the remedy is taking
the wealth they accumulated

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.830
and appropriating it for the government,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.260
which is really just another
name for the things we do

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.230
together like manning 800 military bases

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.490
in over 70 countries and
spending more on defense

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:58.290
than the next 11 nations combined.

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.060
Or wasting half a century punishing people

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.870
for recreational drug use
and putting more Americans

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.050
per capita in prison than
Cuba, Russia, and China.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.310
Or passing massive COVID relief bills

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.760
that only spent 5% of their
totals on actual COVID relief.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:17.240
There are 724 American billionaires,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.140
worth a total of $4.4
trillion, according to Forbes.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.390
It's a list that includes
entertainment moguls

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.750
like Steven Spielberg and Tyler Perry,

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.130
and lawyer in training Kim Kardashian.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:31.750
If it were somehow possible to
liquidate all of that wealth

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.230
without causing a market
crash that would obliterate

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.830
most of it in the process,
we could cover roughly half

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:42.130
a year of combined local,
state and federal spending.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.253
I'm going to ride a rocket into space,

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.640
and it's going to look just like my dick.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.510
Instead of mocking billionaires,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.140
and their penis shaped
rockets millionaires,

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.440
like Jon Stewart and Jason Alexander,

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.650
should take aim at the federal government,

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:00.600
which is the biggest dick in the room

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.700
by a few orders of magnitude.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.870
Our national debt is around $22 trillion

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:08.660
and will continue to climb
in the years to come,

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:12.470
so that by 2050, just
paying interest on the debt,

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:14.050
will account for about a quarter

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.040
of every dollar the
federal government spends.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.120
That kind of debt correlates strongly

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.400
with sharply reduced economic growth,

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.000
which is the only proven way

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.680
of improving living standards over time.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.010
In the years to come, the
US will have no choice,

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.150
but to raise taxes on
everyone, and slash Medicare

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.740
and Social Security, which are
the biggest budget busters.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.160
But, by then, it'll be
too late for a generation

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.490
of elderly people to plan accordingly.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:42.570
And a US debt crisis
could destroy the dollar,

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.840
and undermine our entire economy.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.420
There is no way to
confiscate enough wealth

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.530
to stave off our looming
fiscal catastrophe.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.410
So instead of harping on rich
people and their rockets,

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:56.040
let's start talking about
the looming debt crisis,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.050
fueled by insane government spending,

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:02.483
and come up with an actual
way to avert catastrophe.

